  "notes": "Three unit types, three ways of saying how a character grows. The recruit authors every chance and a level that costs less than a hundred. The veteran authors a partial block: the stats it does not name never roll and never grow, which is a different statement from naming them at zero. The conscript authors nothing at all, which is what every unit type written before growth existed says — worth nothing to defeat, a hundred experience a level, and growing no stat ever. The quarry is the other half: something worth defeating, which is the only way any of the above is ever reached.",
